## 1. Problem Statement & User Friction

### 1.1 User Friction
* **Unnatural 6×2 Keypad Layout:** The legacy layout spans digits across two wide rows of six columns (`1–5 + ⌫` and `6–0 + .`), breaking universal mobile ergonomic conventions and forcing visual searching.
* **Narrow Touch Targets & High Error Rate:** Six columns across mobile screen widths result in cramped touch targets (~50px), driving accidental mis-taps, unintended deletions, and decimal errors during in-play betting.
* **Action Key Clutter:** Top-right placement of the backspace key and non-standard decimal positioning increase cognitive friction and stake correction time.

### 1.2 Business Inefficiency
* **Betslip Abandonment:** Slow stake entry causes customers to miss fast-moving in-play odds or abandon betslips entirely.
* **Conversion Drop-off:** Distance between the keypad and the submission CTA ("Place Bet") introduces thumb repositioning latency, directly hurting final funnel conversion.

---

## 2. Hypothesis & Experiment Matrix

### 2.1 Experiment Hypothesis
Migrating to a standardized 3×4 numeric grid (with enlarged touch targets) combined with bringing the "Place Bet" CTA closer to the natural thumb strike zone will reduce stake entry and correction time, driving a statistically significant uplift in **Betslip Conversion Rate** (`betslip_conversion_rate`) without increasing accidental bet placements.

### 2.2 Variant Definitions (`exp_betslip_keypad_cta_layout`)
| Dimension | Control Group | Variant A (`cta_above`) | Variant B (`cta_below`) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Keypad Grid** | Legacy 2 Rows × 6 Columns | **Standard 4 Rows × 3 Columns** | **Standard 4 Rows × 3 Columns** |
| **Touch Target Width** | ~50px (cramped) | **~100px+ (Thumb Zone)** | **~100px+ (Thumb Zone)** |
| **CTA Placement** | Pinned to bottom of betslip container | Pinned to bottom of betslip container | Pinned to top of betslip container (above the quick stake) |
| **Quick Stake Chips** | Horizontal bar above keypad | Horizontal bar above keypad  | Horizontal bar above keypad  |

