## 3. Success Metrics & Experiment Guardrails

### 3.1 Primary Metric: Betslip Conversion Rate
* **Core Definition:** $\text{Conversion Rate} = \frac{\text{Unique Sessions with Confirmed Bet Placed}}{\text{Unique Sessions with Betslip Opened}} \times 100$
* **Success Criterion:** Statistically significant ($p < 0.05$, 95% confidence interval) uplift in confirmed bet placements for either Variant A or Variant B compared to Control.

### 3.2 Secondary Metrics
* **Stake Entry & Placement Speed:** Measurable reduction in elapsed time from stake input focus to pressing "Place Bet".
* **Correction Frequency:** Reduction of single backspace taps and long-press clears ($\ge 900$ms) per completed bet.
* **In-Play Acceptance Rate:** Percentage of placed bets accepted without odds-change rejections or market suspensions.

### 3.3 Guardrails
* **Immediate Cash-Out Rate:** Cash-outs initiated within 10 seconds of bet confirmation must not increase by $>0.5\%$ (guards against accidental bet placements caused by CTA proximity).
* **Abandonment Rate:** No increase in abandonment after entering the first digit or selecting a quick-stake chip.

